visited >> reported -> optima are found and then dropped from the reported set (a recording problem).
visited ~= reported -> the search itself stops finding new optima.
distinct << |rep|   -> the reported set is mostly duplicates of the same basins.
blocked > 0        -> reported niches are held by points that miss eps, so they score nothing.
PR_res >> PR_now   -> the loss is in the reporting rule: the same run, rescored off a legal
                      cap-sized set reselected from its own history, is worth this much more.
|res| < cap        -> the history held fewer rho-separated points than the cap allows, so the
                      cap is not what limits the reselected set.
